 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "2022-04-07",
   "text": "Pistol Brace Protection Act\n This bill removes certain brace-equipped firearms from regulation under certain federal firearms laws. \n Specifically, under the bill, a pistol that that is equipped with an attachable stabilizing brace (or arm brace) that allows the pistol to be fired with one hand is not a rifle or shotgun subject to regulation (e.g., registration requirements) under the National Firearms Act."
  }
